      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That profound sense of awe from the James Webb Telescope is powerful, but it doesn't make your feelings or daily struggles any less valid. The vastness of the universe often feels lonely, yet human resilience and connection are rare in such darkness. Please remember that the goal is not to compete with galaxies, but to find meaning within your own lived experiences. If today feels heavy for you, it is okay to rest or speak with someone who can offer support.",
